# --- s033 Book I d.8 q.1 = Ord. I d.8 p.1 q.1 (Vat. IV)
n("n570","s033-01","Circa distinctionem octauam","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 1 (ed. Vat. IV), *utrum Deus sit summe simplex*. Cf. Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 8 cc. 3–8.","certain")
n("n571","s033-01","primo phicorum","la","source","Aristotle, *Phys.* I.3, 186a34–b4: *quod vere est* (Parmenides' *ens*) is not an accident of anything (*nulli accidit*), in the medieval *auctoritas* form.","certain")
n("n572","s033-01","Aug. 6. de trini. c. 6.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* VI 6.8: God is *vere summeque simplex*. B reads *Aug. vi. de tri. deus summe simplex est*, without the chapter number (B checked).","certain")
n("n573","s033-02","Aug. 5. de trini.","la","source","The equality of the Holy Spirit *per summam simplicitatem* is in Augustine, *De Trin.* VI 7.9 (B, like A, has *v.*, B checked). The locus is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n574","s033-03","simplex est quod non est resolubile","la","source","On the simply simple concept (*conceptus simpliciter simplex*) as the term of resolution, see Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 1 qq. 1–2 nn. 71–73, and *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 1.","to-verify")
n("n575","s033-06","sunt octo modi ydemptitatis","la","source","The graded list of eight modes of identity (from the persons' properties up to the essence with its *summum esse*) is not in this form in Scotus's *Ordinatio*. Lists of modes of identity and distinction are characteristic of later Scotists, notably Francis of Meyronnes (*Conflatus* I d. 8). This source is a conjecture to be checked.","conjecture")
n("n576","s033-06","sed differunt ex natura rei","la","textual","After *idem realiter essentialiter et formaliter*, the clause *differunt ex natura rei* seems contradictory, since Scotus's formal distinction is *ex natura rei*. Perhaps *non formaliter* or *modaliter* is meant, as in Scotus's doctrine of intrinsic modes (*Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 3 nn. 138–140). Kept as printed.","uncertain")
n("n577","s033-07","tertio modo dicendi per se","la","source","Aristotle, *APo.* I.4, 73b5–8: the third mode of *per se*, being by itself (*solitarium*), as substance, not said of a subject.","certain")
n("n578","s033-07","melius quam non ipsum","la","source","Anselm, *Monologion* c. 15: a *perfectio simpliciter* is *quod omnino melius est ipsum quam non ipsum*. Scotus discusses the definition at *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 3 and *Quodl.* q. 5.","certain")
n("n579","s033-03","The simply simple","en","translation","Gorris uses three grades: *simplex* (irresolvable but composable), *simpliciter simplex* (the term of resolution, e.g. *ens*), and *summe simplex* (neither resolvable nor composable: God alone).")
n("n580","s033-07","pure perfection","en","translation","*perfectio simpliciter*: the standard rendering ‘pure perfection’.")
n("n581","s033-07","does not [so] truly “be”","en","translation","The Latin (*sed in deo non vere est*) is compressed. The point is that wisdom in God is not a *per se* subsistent in the third mode, so the *auctoritas* does not apply.","uncertain")

# --- B collation (full): B48L–B49L
upd("n572", append=" B also lacks the chapter number (*Aug. vi. de tri. deus summe simplex est*).")
n("n957","s033-03","sed est componibile alteri vt ens","la","textual","B omits everything from this clause to the second *vltimata resolutio* (*sed est componibile… stat vltimata resolutio*). It reads *Sed ipsum extat vltimata resolutio. nec est componibile alteri*, which is an eye-skip and runs the definitions of *simplex* and *summe simplex* together.","certain")
n("n958","s033-03","sunt componibilia","la","textual","B: *sunt incomponibilia*. This is against the sense: creatures are not supremely simple because they are composable.","certain")
n("n959","s033-04","natura humana et diuina","la","textual","B: *creatura humana et diuina*.","certain")
n("n960","s033-04","vel tres persone sunt distincte","la","textual","B omits *vel tres persone… summa simplicitate* (eye-skip from *simplicitate* to *simplicitate*).","certain")
upd("n576", append=" B has the same reading (*sed differunt ex natura rei*).")
n("n961","s033-07","ipsum esse est","la","textual","B: *ipsum est melius quam ipsum. i. non quolibet suo incompossibili*. *non* has been misplaced, and A's reading is the right one (Anselm's *melius ipsum quam non ipsum*).","certain")
